Negative control for the per-row capability gate (C11).

Ignores the action's declared RULE, so every control renders live on every row
— the defect where the UI offers Remove on a row the API says cannot be
deleted, and the user learns the business rule from a server rejection.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: list-surface-capability-gate.spec.ts — the `meta.canDelete === false`
case (the control must be disabled).

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
@@ -613,7 +613,7 @@
       placement: action.placement,
       // The precondition is the ROW's own — a rule over the meta the record
       // itself carries, never a client-side guess about what the API allows.
-      disabled: !isRuleEnabled(action, row) || feedback.isPending(control),
+      disabled: feedback.isPending(control),
       onSelect: () =>
         action.handoff
           ? openHandoff(action, row)
